 "title": "Friedel–Crafts acylation of benzene",
 "caption": "AlCl₃ generates the acylium ion CH₃CO⁺ from ethanoyl chloride. The delocalised π electrons attack it, breaking aromaticity in the arenium ion; AlCl₄⁻ removes the proton from the sp³ carbon, restoring the ring and regenerating AlCl₃. The product is phenylethanone.",
 "alt": "Three stages: benzene's ring attacking the acylium ion; AlCl₄⁻ removing a proton from the arenium ion; phenylethanone, HCl and AlCl₃.",
 "description": [
  "Stage 1: a curly arrow from the ring's π electrons to the positive carbon of the acylium ion, CH₃C⁺=O.",
  "Stage 2: the arenium ion with a horseshoe; a curly arrow from an Al–Cl bond of AlCl₄⁻ to the ring hydrogen, and one from the C–H bond back into the ring.",
  "Stage 3: phenylethanone, HCl and AlCl₃ (the catalyst is regenerated)."
